  "term": "synesthesia",
  "definition": "Synesthesia is a condition in which one kind of stimulus automatically and involuntarily triggers an additional sensory or perceptual experience. A common example is experiencing colors in response to letters, numbers, words, or music, though other combinations of senses can also occur.",
